409.description:
The member cannot get the phone yet; `code` says why:
- `not_set_up`: the organization is not set up for the phone (see getManagerStatus);
- `identity_subject_unavailable`: identity-api cannot issue the member's subject (organization
  not enabled on the identity client, or the user is not an active member there);
- `identity_client_unavailable`: the identity client the setup points at is not active;
- `provider_conflict`: the provider refused, e.g. this person's identity is bound to another
  provider user.

EligibilityPath.description:
How an agent can take a queue's calls:
- `skill`: the queue routes to people with a skill the agent has (changes with the agent's skills);
- `direct`: the agent is in the queue's epilot-managed step (added from the control center);
- `routing`: the phone system's own routing names the agent (a team or a person set up there);
  epilot does not change it.
